    "created_at": "2026-08-13T18:46:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-13T18:46:30Z",
    "body": "Addressed in the ranex fork (ranex-trim): the shell tool now guards the parse-error / zero-command permission bypass. Root cause: a trailing double-dash (or other malformed input) makes tree-sitter-powershell emit an ERROR node with zero command descendants, and a clean-parse zero-command input (comment/redirection-only) also yields zero command nodes — so collect() produced empty scan.patterns and ask() early-returned before any permission rule was evaluated (beating configured deny AND ask). Fix: on tree.rootNode.hasError OR commands(root).length===0, replace the scan with the raw command so the permission check always fires; valid parses untouched. Commit 2d0950f6e5 (merged to ranex-trim). Supersedes the narrower hasError-only guard; applies upstream.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
